The scoring state machines and regression cases are adapted from chardetng
1.0.0, copyright Mozilla Foundation, under the MIT license option.
See META-INF/LICENSES/Chardetng-MIT.txt in the published archives.
Source: https://github.com/hsivonen/chardetng/tree/v1.0.0

The character-class maps, pair scores, and CJK frequency lists are derived
from src/data.rs, dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

This port uses JDK charset decoders and rejects malformed or unmappable
input for each candidate. It does not emulate encoding_rs decoding tables
or the upstream allowances for unsupported Macintosh and vendor extensions.
It uses the generic-domain selection rules, without browser domain hints.
